  "reviews": [
    {
      "date": "2026-07-29",
      "reason": "PERF-5: first population. Counters and ceilings recorded from the honest instrument at b7f5fc7 (PERF-4a); before this the file was `{}` and gated nothing."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-14",
      "reason": "render-web ceiling raised 24195 -> 40947 B. Owner-authorized. The package took explicit ownership of the WebGL context (GetWebGLContext/MakeWebGLContext/MakeOnScreenGLSurface + paired teardown), gained webglcontextlost/restored self-healing, and its CanvasKit loader gained stall-abort, deadline and retry-after-failure. Added behaviour, not a regression. Note for future triage: source maps are ~61% of this package's gzipped dist (23254 B of 38242 B, summing per-file gzip of index.js.map, index.mjs.map, index.d.ts.map, index.d.mts.map against the full dist/), so byte growth here tracks source-map growth more than code growth."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-15",
      "reason": "New package @flare-engine/dynamics: ceiling CREATED at 37650 B (measured 34227 B, the standard 10% headroom). Creating a missing ceiling is the safe direction --write is allowed to take; no existing ceiling was raised (the run reported 1 created, 0 tightened, 41 left alone). The same `--write --bytes` run also refreshed `measured`/`measuredAt` fleet-wide to current reality — most are unchanged, audio fell 13565 -> 13522 B (a dead private field was removed) and core rose 20675 -> 21319 B with no source change in that package, which is pack-metadata drift rather than code growth. Counter scenarios were rewritten with identical values (no diff). Known-red at this commit and NOT addressed here: check:perf-freshness, which reports the published benchmark numbers as stale because commit 6a10aa9 (Vec2.perp/crossSV) changed sources that the ECS, Physics, Particles, Render and Integration suites transitively measure. Clearing it needs an owner-run recapture from a clean, quiet tree (bun run bench x5, bench:promote, bench:md) — an agent-run capture on a loaded machine would publish contended numbers, which is the failure mode PERF-1/PERF-5 exist to prevent."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-25",
      "reason": "react ceiling raised 51558 -> 66349 B. Owner-authorized. Arc WEB: scene-texture.ts (the reused offscreen surface + depth-3 frame-image retention ring) plus GameView's web capture path and postfx gate. packages/react/src grew 35305 -> 46541 B (+31.8%) across exactly two files (scene-texture.ts new, game-view.tsx +54/-9); packed measured 46870 -> 60317 B (+28.7%), consistent with that. Same dynamic as the 2026-08-14 render-web note: 57% of this package's gzipped dist is source maps (36166 of 63397 B), so byte growth here tracks source growth rather than code growth. Externals verified — react, react-native, @shopify/react-native-skia, react-native-safe-area-context and every @flare-engine/* dep are require()d, not inlined. Added behaviour, not a regression."
    }
  ]
}
